                <pb facs="0474" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3533: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-27T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>288. Your telegram 367, October 22, 4 p.m. By whom was suggestion made that
                    control over proceeds of increased customs duties should be vested in Minister
                    of Finance, Inspector General of Customs and Bankers’ Association?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
